{"id":"u-7800ac7c-27d6-41ad-bd24-d452fa0ef9ba","src":"community","title":"First Pull-Up and Legs Training Program","author":"Bully Strength","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/Ky6MF0-bailey-training-program","desc":"Focus on:\n- Developing legs\n- Developing back\n- Foundation in key movements: squat, pull-ups, Romanian deadlift, unilateral work, etc.\n- Working toward first pull-up\n\nYou can add in 5-10 minutes of core as needed.\n\n\n\nImportant Information: \n\n“RPE”\n\nRPE = Rate of Perceived Exertion\n\nThis is a scale used in programming to gauge proximity to failure. For our case, failure means a degradation in form and/or true momentary muscular failure (sloppy rep and/or failed rep).\n\nThe number is always /10. The number refers to 10 minus the RIR (reps in reserve). This is quite subjective and requires experience with failing reps (which is safe as long as safety is considered before set)\n\nRep Scheme:\n\nRanges - most compounds and key movements will give you ranges to work in. Best way to do this is to push for a challenging first set at the top end of the rep range. If you keep the desired effort in mind, the following sets should be fewer reps.\n\nex: 6-10 rep range; set 1 = 10 reps @ RPE 8, set 2 = 9 reps @ RPE 8, set 3 = 7 reps @ RPE 8. Each time it should take fewer reps to get to 8/10 difficulty, thus the decrease in reps over all three sets.\n\nIf you’re able to do 8 reps the next set, note that and consider bumping the weight up for the following set and/or next week.\n\n\n\nDisclaimer:\n\nThis is a personalized program with a particular person’s goals in mind when programming and likely is not going to exactly fit the needs of every individual.\n\nAnticipated flaws are: lack of core work, lack of cardio work, likely not enough pressing volume, and heavily favoring leg and back volume.\n\nWhile I am normally the first to say women should structure their splits extremely similar to how men’s programs would, this program keeps in mind the requests of the original person and the typical goals/requests from dozens of women clients. Modifications can be made.","level":["Beginner"],"goals":["Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":80,"joins":6,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-09-19T12:13:09.933Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3","Day 4"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Seated Bike","sets":[{"sec":300}]},{"n":"Band Pass-Through","sets":[{"r":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"Inverted Row","sets":[{"r":8},{"r":12},{"r":0,"rpe":9}],"note":"TRX or barbell on a rack"},{"ss":[{"n":"Scapular Pull-Up","sets":[{"r":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Eccentric Pull-Up","sets":[{"r":6,"x":3}]}]},{"n":"Incline Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Row (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Single Arm Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Seated Bike","sets":[{"sec":300}]},{"n":"Banded Side Steps","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":20,"x":2}]},{"n":"Heel Tap Step Downs","sets":[{"r":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Leg Press","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bulgarian Split Squat (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":6,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Hip Abductor (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"x":2}]},{"n":"Hip Adductor (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"x":2}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Calf Raise (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":2}]},{"n":"Tibialis Raise","sets":[{"lo":20,"hi":30,"x":2}]}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Seated Bike","sets":[{"sec":300}]},{"n":"Band Pass-Through","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":15,"x":2}]},{"n":"I, Y, T (IYT) Raise","sets":[{"r":6,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lu Raise","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Seated Bike","sets":[{"sec":300}]},{"n":"Band Pass-Through","sets":[{